#: manual/tutorial/parser.md:111
msgid "Read a theorem script"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/parser.md:113
msgid "A theorem script parses into a header, a goal and a list of steps with their positions. This is the `demo_and` script from `examples/demo_and.qed`:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/parser.md:131
msgid "Step indices count every step in reading order, including those inside branches: `intro` is 1, `split` is 2, the first `exact` is 3 and the second is 4. The prover reports failures with these numbers."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/parser.md:135
msgid "**Lower a quantified goal.** `forall` is accepted at the start of a goal and lowered as a theorem-header binder: the bound name becomes a free variable of the goal."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/parser.md:146
msgid "**Keep identities.** `parse_resolved_term` and `parse_resolved_goal_with_env` return `elab` terms with constant identities frozen; use them when terms are stored and checked later, as the [elab tutorial](elab.md) explains."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/parser.md:148
msgid "**Define functions from text.** `parse_def_function(state, env, \"def id(x : bool) : bool { x }\")` admits a definition through the kernel and returns its theorem; see the [parser API](../api/parser.md)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/parser.md:150
msgid "**Run the script.** Parsing a script does not prove it. Pass the source text to the [prover](prover.md), which lowers the goal, runs each step with the [tactics](tactics.md) package and reports failures with the spans you saw above."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/parser.md:154
msgid "**Old connective spellings.** `/\\` and `\\/` are not accepted; use `∧`, `∨` or `\\and`, `\\or`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/parser.md:155
msgid "**Chained equality.** `a = b = c` is a `NonAssocChain` error; add parentheses."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/parser.md:156
msgid "**Quantifiers in terms.** `forall` is only allowed at the start of a goal. `parse_term` rejects it with a `Parse` error."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/parser.md:157
msgid "**Missing turnstile.** A goal needs `⊢` or `|-`, even with no hypotheses: write `⊢ T`, not `T`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/parser.md:158
msgid "**`T` and `F` without the prelude.** They are constants, not keywords; without `install_prop_prelude` they are unknown names."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/parser.md:159
msgid "**Connectives on non-propositions.** `f ∧ p` with `f : bool -> bool` fails at lowering with `Logic(NotBoolTerm)`."
msgstr ""

