msgid "When a step fails, the result says which step, on which branch, with which goal and locals. This is `examples/bad_branch.qed`:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/prover.md:84
msgid "Step 3 is `exact truth` (after `intro h` and `left`), on branch 1 of the `left` block. The goal at that point is `x`, which `truth` does not prove."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/prover.md:86
msgid "Report an unfinished proof"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/prover.md:88
msgid "A `hole` marks a gap. The prover stops there and reports the goal the hole stands for; no theorem is produced. This is `examples/unfinished_branch.qed`:"
msgstr ""

