msgid "`prove_theorem_file_results_detailed` checks every theorem of a file and keeps going after a failure or a hole. This is `examples/multi_with_hole.qed`:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/prover.md:137
msgid "**Run against your own state.** Pass `@prover.prover_options(false)` to skip the prelude and run against a state you prepared, for example one with extra constants declared through the kernel. Without the prelude, `T` is unknown and the run fails with a `Sig` diagnostic:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/prover.md:149
msgid "**Use the corpus.** `positive_corpus_cases()` and its siblings return the scripts the tests run, with their expected outcomes. They are a ready-made set of examples and a regression suite for anything you build on top of the prover."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/prover.md:151
msgid "**Render results.** The [cmd](cmd.md) package turns these results into the `ok`, `error[...]` and `warning[unfinished]` lines of the command-line tool; reuse its renderer if you need the same text."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/prover.md:155
msgid "**Expecting theorems from holes.** An `Unfinished` result has no theorem, and `prove_theorem_script` returns it as an error."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/prover.md:156
msgid "**Citing earlier theorems.** Theorems proved earlier in a file are not available to later ones; only catalog names are."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/prover.md:157
msgid "**Forgetting `qed` between theorems.** In a file with several theorems, each one but possibly the last must be followed by a `qed` line, or the file fails to parse."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/prover.md:158
msgid "**Free names in goals.** A name in a goal must be a header binder, a constant of the state, or `T`/`F` from the prelude. Use binders such as `(x : bool)` for variables."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/prover.md:159
msgid "**Raw `forall` inside terms.** `forall` is accepted only at the start of the goal."
msgstr ""

